From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] guarded windows deleted while a screen changes its DPI

QGuiApplicationPrivate::processScreenLogicalDotsPerInchChange() emits
screenChanged() for every window on the screen whose logical DPI changed
(added by the backported DPI change fixes). It iterates a raw pointer
snapshot of QGuiApplication::allWindows(), and each emission synchronously
runs application code and the geometry change processing it triggers.
That code is free to close and delete other windows, so entries later in
the snapshot can already be freed when the loop calls screen() on them.

This was seen live on Windows: the crash lands in the loop reading the
screen of a window that was destroyed by an earlier iteration.

Hold the snapshot through QPointer and skip windows destroyed during the
loop, the same way the leftover window loop on the screen removal path is
already guarded. Every live window on the screen still gets screenChanged().

diff --git a/src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp b/src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp
index f88d6fe8..5f85ec0b 100644
--- a/src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp
@@ -3204,9 +3204,21 @@ void QGuiApplicationPrivate::processScreenLogicalDotsPerInchChange(QWindowSystem
     emit s->logicalDotsPerInchChanged(s->logicalDotsPerInch());
     s->d_func()->updateGeometriesWithSignals();
 
-    for (QWindow *window : QGuiApplication::allWindows())
-        if (window->screen() == e->screen)
+    // Patched: screenChanged() runs application code synchronously (and the
+    // geometry change it triggers delivers further events), and that code is
+    // free to close and delete other windows still waiting in this snapshot.
+    // allWindows() hands out raw pointers, so hold them through QPointer and
+    // re-check every one before it is dereferenced.
+    const auto allWindows = QGuiApplication::allWindows();
+    QList<QPointer<QWindow>> windows;
+    windows.reserve(allWindows.size());
+    for (QWindow *window : allWindows)
+        windows.append(window);
+    for (const QPointer<QWindow> &guard : windows) {
+        QWindow *window = guard.data();
+        if (window && window->screen() == e->screen)
             window->screenChanged(e->screen);
+    }
 
     resetCachedDevicePixelRatio();
 }
